---
title: Overview
description: What CRM covers — opportunities, the sales pipeline, reports and contracts — and who does what.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

CRM follows each piece of potential work from the first contact to the signed contract. Every lead is an **opportunity** on the board; it moves through the firm's pipeline stages until it is won, lost or cancelled. The dashboard reports on the pipeline and on the sales targets, and Operon reminds the person in charge of deals that have stopped moving.

Contracts are prepared on an opportunity. The person in charge picks the services on the opportunity, and Operon builds the contract from the firm's template: the scope and fee sections list exactly the services picked, at the agreed prices. A discounted contract goes to the department lead for approval. The firm always signs with its signatory's saved signature; the client signs online or on paper. Every file of the deal stays with the opportunity, and once the client pays, the signed services open their cases.

## The stages of a contract

| Stage | What happens |
|---|---|
| **1 Prepare** | Choose the client, the client signatory, the issuing entity, the language and the format. |
| **2 Draft** | Read the generated contract through; edit the wording if needed. |
| **3 Approval** | Only when needed: a discount above the firm's threshold, or a draft edited by hand. |
| **4 Signing** | Send for e-signature, or record a copy signed on paper. |
| **5 Signed** | The signed copy is filed with the opportunity. The services can be invoiced and delivered. |

## Who does what

| Role | Work |
|---|---|
| **Person in charge (PIC)** | Works the deal: keeps its details and stage up to date, writes notes and follows up. Picks the services and prices, prepares and generates the contract, submits it and sends it for signing. |
| **Manager in charge** | Oversees the deal. Receives the follow-up reminders when the deal has no PIC. |
| **Director in charge** | Oversees the deal and signs contracts for the firm. The firm's signature on a contract is always the saved signature of the opportunity's Director in charge. |
| **Team lead** | Sets up the stages and vocabularies, and sets personal sales targets. Named by the tenant admin in the CRM settings. |
| **Department lead** | A user with the department lead permission set. Keeps the department's services, packages, prices, payment terms and contract wording up to date. Approves discounted contracts. |
| **Tenant admin** | Decides who can use CRM and who sees all opportunities. Maintains the contract settings, the issuing entities, the contract signatories with their saved signatures, and the contract templates. Approves a contract that a department lead submitted. |

